Vitruvian Courier (apps/desktop/vitruvian-courier): route Google Messages events by the IDs Google nests them
under when the top-level ones are empty, and never let one empty ID become a chat.

Google now sends some messages and conversation updates with the top-level message ID (field 1) and conversation
ID (field 7) empty, and the real ones nested (field 23 carries the conversation ID, field 24 the message ID, field
35 a conversation's latest message ID). v0.2609.0 keyed the chat on the top-level ID alone: every such event landed
in one chat with an empty conversation ID ("1."), messages with the same empty ID overwrote each other as edits,
and deduplicateDM, seeing a contact's phone on that chat, re-ID'd the contact's real portal into it. That deleted the
real portal and tombstoned its room, and the mapping update after it failed (its first write used the outer
context, not the transaction's) with the error thrown away, so the mapping kept pointing at a portal that no longer
existed.

This backports the nested-ID fallback of upstream mautrix-gmessages #166 (b580a1a, fillMissingIDs; also for typing
notices) and the dedup fixes on upstream main (the transaction's context, the error returned), and adds what
neither has:
- the portal move now comes after the mapping is stored, and puts the mapping back if the move fails, so a failure
  can't leave a deleted portal with a mapping to it;
- an event that has no conversation ID even after the fallback (or a message with no message ID) is dropped with
  an error log, in libgm and again in the connector; deduplicateDM refuses a conversation with no ID and never
  moves a portal out of an empty-ID one.

Neither upstream change is in v0.2609.0 or v0.2610.0. Drop this patch when a release has both. Written against
the tree with mautrix-gmessages-conversation-read-receipt.patch applied: keep it after that one in MODULE.bazel.

